1
00:04:52,173 --> 00:04:58,173
How far would you go for a friend?

2
00:09:44,347 --> 00:09:50,347
Free Willy is a family, adventure, drama film directed by Simon Wincer.

3
00:14:36,521 --> 00:14:42,521
When maladjusted orphan Jesse vandalizes a theme park, he is placed with
foster parents and must work at the park to make amends.

4
00:19:28,695 --> 00:19:34,695
There he meets Willy, a young Orca whale who has been separated from his family.

5
00:24:20,869 --> 00:24:26,869
Sensing kinship, they form a bond and, with the help of kindly whale
trainer Rae Lindley, develop a routine of tricks.

6
00:29:13,043 --> 00:29:19,043
However, greedy park owner Dial soon catches wind of the
duo and makes plans to profit from them.

7
00:34:05,217 --> 00:34:11,217
Jesse, played by Jason James Richter.

8
00:38:57,391 --> 00:39:03,391
Willy, played by Keiko.

9
00:43:49,565 --> 00:43:55,565
Rae Lindley, played by Lori Petty.

10
00:48:41,739 --> 00:48:47,739
Randolph Johnson, played by August Schellenberg.

11
00:53:33,913 --> 00:53:39,913
Glen Greenwood, played by Michael Madsen.

12
00:58:26,086 --> 00:58:32,086
Annie Greenwood, played by Jayne Atkinson.

13
01:03:18,260 --> 01:03:24,260
Free Willy is a 1993 family drama film, directed by Simon Wincer, produced by Lauren Shuler Donner and Jennie Lew
Tugend, written by Keith Walker and Corey Blechman from a story by Walker and distributed by Warner Bros.

14
01:08:10,434 --> 01:08:16,434
Pictures under their Family Entertainment imprint.

15
01:13:02,608 --> 01:13:08,608
The film stars Jason James Richter in his film debut, Lori Petty, Jayne Atkinson, August
Schellenberg, and Michael Madsen with the eponymous character, Willy, played by Keiko.

16
01:17:54,782 --> 01:18:00,782
The story is about a 12-year-old orphaned boy named Jesse who
befriends a captive orca, Willy, at an ailing amusement park.

17
01:22:46,956 --> 01:22:52,956
When he discovers that the park owner has been planning to dispose of
Willy, he hatches a scheme to break Willy out of captivity.

18
01:27:39,130 --> 01:27:45,130
Released on July 16, 1993, the film received positive attention from critics and was a
commercial success, grossing $153.7 million from a $20 million budget.

19
01:32:31,304 --> 01:32:37,304
It grew into a small franchise, including an animated television series, two sequels, and a
direct-to-video reboot in addition to inspiring the rehabilitation and release of Keiko.

20
01:37:23,478 --> 01:37:29,478
The film marked Keith Walker's only film as screenwriter, and
last project before his death on December 30, 1996.

21
01:42:15,652 --> 01:42:21,652
The film explores themes of whale, social worker, freedom,
social work, human animal relationship.

22
01:47:07,826 --> 01:47:13,826
The tone is emotional.
